\details{
Verified against \code{urca::ur.df} and \code{MASS::rlm}.  The ADF
statistic is not t-distributed under the null, so it must be compared
with the Dickey-Fuller critical values returned here rather than normal
ones; large negative values reject the unit root.  \code{morie_rlm}
estimates the scale as \code{mad(resid, 0)/0.6745}, the MAD about
zero, which is what MASS does -- centring it on the residual median
instead shifts every weight.  The same functions exist in the Python
package as \code{morie.fn._robust_core}.
}
